      "properties": {
        "reported": true,
        "property_type": "optical",
        "summary": "In CH3CN, 2 exhibits ligand-centered emission at 514 nm and NIR Nd(III) bands at 882, 1067 and 1335 nm. Lifetime 6.78 μs; intrinsic ΦLn 2.7%; overall Φem 0.12%. It shows rapid ratiometric fluorescence sensing of quercetin (Que) by quenching both ligand-centered and Nd emissions (KSV 2.9×10^4 and 3.8×10^4 M−1; LOD 6.75 and 2.03 μM), linear I1067/I514 vs [Que], ~5 s response, and little interference from tested biomolecules/ions. Quenching is attributed to inner-filter effect and ligand-to-Que energy transfer, mainly static (lifetime 6.71 μs at 120 μM Que).",
